WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.800
When it comes to raw power, nothing&nbsp;
gives a devil fruit user the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:11.680
edge like a zoan fruit. But which of&nbsp;
these fruits is the most beastly of all?

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.920
Today we’re counting down the top 5&nbsp;
strongest zoan devil fruits in One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.680
but quick spoiler warning for some&nbsp;
very recently revealed fruits!

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.720
First off, what’s a zoan in the first place?&nbsp;
This category of fruits allows its users to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:31.760
transform into various animals. From cobras, to&nbsp;
falcons, to allosauruses these fruits bestow the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.840
greatest raw strength, endurance, and speed&nbsp;
of any fruit category. They even include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:44.160
ancient and mythical subsets - ancient zoans being&nbsp;
based on extinct creatures and mythical zoans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.320
the rarest of all fruits, being&nbsp;
based on mythological figures.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:56.240
And no surprise here, #5 is a mythical zoan:&nbsp;
The Inu Inu no Mi: Model Okuchi no Makami.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:03.440
Yamato has only been in the series for a short&nbsp;
while, but is already a fan favorite character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.160
And they have already proven themselves to have&nbsp;
one of the most powerful fruits in the series -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:14.880
the guardian deity of Wano, the Okuchi no Makami,&nbsp;
that can even go toe to toe with Kaidou himself.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.120
So…how did we decide this anyway? Well,&nbsp;
this ranking isn’t arbitrary. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.480
we’ve chosen our devil fruit rankings in a&nbsp;
highly scientific manner. In an exhaustive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.320
and time-consuming process,&nbsp;
we’ve given all of the series’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:36.880
139 devil fruits a score out of 100&nbsp;
based on six different criteria.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.840
First: Strength. What kind of raw&nbsp;
power does the devil fruit have?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.480
How effectively can this&nbsp;
fruit attack its opponents?

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.920
Second, Endurance: Does this fruit&nbsp;
offer any defensive capabilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.040
or resistances against the attacks of others?

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.320
Third, Special Abilities: Besides general&nbsp;
combat prowess, does this fruit have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.400
any secondary abilities worth awarding&nbsp;
points? To illustrate an example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.760
Miss Merry Christmas’s mole fruit wouldn’t&nbsp;
have a ton of strength or endurance, but its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.120
tunneling abilities would give it&nbsp;
several points in this category.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:19.280
The fourth category is Everyday Use:&nbsp;
Let’s say that hypothetically you had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:26.160
this power in real life - how useful&nbsp;
would it be in non-combat situations?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.360
Would the power come in handy even if you&nbsp;
weren’t engaged in intense pirate battles?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.520
Each of these four categories was given a score&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.080
out of 25 for a grand total of&nbsp;
100 available points. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.840
there are two additional categories that&nbsp;
can deduct points from these scores.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.880
Firstly, we have Weaknesses: A great example&nbsp;
for a weakness is Enel’s natural weakness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:56.320
against rubber. If there are any glaring&nbsp;
weaknesses like this, points can be deducted.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.800
Second in the negative categories are&nbsp;
Drawbacks. Are there any problems that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.240
arise from having this fruit? An&nbsp;
example here would be Whitebeard’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:12.080
Quake-Quake fruit. Even though it has immense&nbsp;
raw power, it also has a high chance of causing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:18.640
collateral damage to your own allies. Therefore,&nbsp;
it would lose a few points in this category.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.200
**Back to Yamato’s fruit, the Okuchi&nbsp;
no Makami. With a total of 75 points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.680
let’s look at how it earned the #5 spot.**

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:34.000
For both strength and endurance, the Makami earned&nbsp;
20 points each. With strength and durability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.640
it’s important to factor in a user’s haki as&nbsp;
well. Yamato can go toe to toe with Kaidou,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:47.360
but a lot of that is due to their haki ability&nbsp;
and not necessarily the fruit itself. For these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.440
point totals, we based Yamato’s stats&nbsp;
off of the strength and endurance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:57.680
a wolf. While Yamato’s fruit is strong,&nbsp;
a wolf doesn’t have the same kind of raw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.960
strength or defense that for instance a&nbsp;
dinosaur or elephant would have. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:09.280
a wolf is still a fierce predator and&nbsp;
earns a lot of points in these areas.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:15.200
What helped the Okuchi no Makami beat out a lot of&nbsp;
other fruits, though, are its special abilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:21.920
Having additional ice powers, almost like a bonus&nbsp;
paramecia fruit on top of the benefits of a zoan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:30.000
helped Yamato earn 20 points in the Special&nbsp;
Abilities category. This category yields great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.320
benefits to mythical zoans, who get all sorts&nbsp;
of powers in addition to their transformations.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:41.200
For Everyday Use, Yamato earns 15&nbsp;
points - having the speed, agility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.560
and strength of a wolf could certainly come&nbsp;
in handy in all sorts of situations. And hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.040
those ice powers are going to&nbsp;
come in handy on a hot summer day.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.120
It’s not the most useful fruit outside of combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.440
but you will have the frostiest&nbsp;
beverages in all of Wano.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:06.480
With the Makami, there are no downsides&nbsp;
either, so Yamato doesn’t lose any points.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:15.040
**On to number #4. Ryu Ryu no Mi:&nbsp;
Model Pteranodon. Total Points: 86**

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.400
King’s fruit and other ancient zoans are among the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.280
toughest of the tough when it comes to&nbsp;
strength and endurance. In these categories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:31.040
King earned a 23 in each. You can’t get much&nbsp;
stronger than a dinosaur - so the Pteranodon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.480
earns more points in these categories&nbsp;
than fruits like giraffes or leopards.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.880
What sets the Pteranodon over the edge and&nbsp;
makes it one of the greatest zoan fruits of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:53.120
all is its special ability: flight. Any flying&nbsp;
fruit automatically scores big points for both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:59.920
special abilities and everyday use. In both of&nbsp;
these areas, King scores 20 points. Flying grants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:05.520
huge advantages in combat, and it also helps a&nbsp;
fruit user circumvent a lot of the drowning risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:11.760
that comes with having a devil fruit because they&nbsp;
can simply fly above the ocean. Very convenient.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:17.760
Not only that, but just like Pteranodons&nbsp;
did in the Cretaceous Period, the user of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:23.440
this fruit can stretch their face backward in&nbsp;
order to launch devastating projectile attacks.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.800
And as for everyday use, do I&nbsp;
really have to explain that? I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.480
who among us would not love&nbsp;
to have the power of flight?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.960
As for disadvantages, King loses no points. Lucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.440
for him, there aren’t really any&nbsp;
downsides to being a Pteranodon.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:52.240
**#3. Uo Uo no Mi: Model Seiryu&nbsp;
(Azure Dragon). Total points: 90**

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:58.480
Beating out his first mate for the #3 spot is&nbsp;
Kaidou himself. Of course the world’s strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:04.880
creature had to be on this list. Kaidou&nbsp;
scored perfect marks in the strength and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:10.400
endurance categories. He also had perfect marks&nbsp;
in the special abilities category - he has the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:19.360
same flight as King as well as flame clouds that&nbsp;
can lift entire islands. He also utilizes blast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:25.840
breaths and all sorts of other special, unique&nbsp;
techniques. It seems like the longer Wano goes on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.720
the more special powers Kaidou pulls out. He&nbsp;
gets 20 points for Everyday Use as well because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.200
again, flight would just be&nbsp;
fantastic to have in real life.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:43.120
However, this is the first fruit where a&nbsp;
drawback comes into play. Many fruits don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:49.040
have any drawbacks whatsoever, but there’s one&nbsp;
big one I can think of when it comes to Kaidou.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:57.440
He’s massive. Just absolutely huge. Which is&nbsp;
great, until you want to fight someone *indoors*.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:05.680
During the raid on Onigashima, he had no&nbsp;
choice but to take things outside with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:12.000
Akazaya 9. His unwieldy size makes him so&nbsp;
destructive that he’s at risk of destroying things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.360
he doesn’t want to destroy, such as his own home.&nbsp;
This is great when you’re attacking an enemy base,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:24.080
but not so great during an enemy raid.&nbsp;
For this drawback, Kaidou loses 5 points.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:30.720
There’s also some speculation that Kaidou’s fruit&nbsp;
wasn’t so useful when he first got it. As we know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:37.360
his fruit is not a Dragon fruit, but a Fish&nbsp;
fruit. It’s possible that he only achieved his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:42.444
current strength after a Magikarp-esque&nbsp;
ordeal. However, until we get the long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.444 --> 00:08:46.480
awaited Kaidou flashback, we can’t allow&nbsp;
this theory to affect Kaidou’s score.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:10:00.240
**Up next might be a surprise to many of you who&nbsp;
may have expected this fruit to be number 1. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:09.360
94 points, we have #2: Monkey D. Luffy’s&nbsp;
fruit - the Hito Hito no Mi: Model Nika.**

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:15.520
This is a fruit we’ve known for a long time but&nbsp;
have only just learned is a mythical zoan. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:22.800
hard to rate given that we haven’t seen the&nbsp;
full extent of its abilities, but clearly its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:30.640
endurance is off the charts. Luffy’s pliable,&nbsp;
rubber body can take beating after beating.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.960
Its strength is also maxed out given&nbsp;
the ability to deliver just about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:40.640
any attack one can imagine. Punching with&nbsp;
a fist the size of an island comes to mind.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:46.480
Its special abilities are, of course, also&nbsp;
crazy and I’m sure we’ve only scratched the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:51.840
surface of what Oda has planned for the fruit.&nbsp;
So far, we’ve seen Luffy throwing lightning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:57.120
and imbuing both the ground and his opponent with&nbsp;
rubber-like qualities as well. These, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:02.240
are on top of the wide range of abilities&nbsp;
that Luffy utilized in his base form and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:09.280
the other gears. So for each of the first&nbsp;
three categories, this fruit earns 25 points.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:16.800
Everyday use gets 20 points - a considerable&nbsp;
score, but not maxed out. He can fly in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.840
roundabout, bouncy sort of way. He can&nbsp;
reach hard to reach places. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:26.960
it just doesn’t have the kind of practical&nbsp;
usage that we see from some other fruits.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:33.840
It does, however, lose a small number of&nbsp;
points. Unlike a lot devil fruits that don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:39.280
have a specific weakness, all the way since East&nbsp;
Blue it’s been stated that Luffy is vulnerable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:44.720
to blades and cutting attacks. Recently, even&nbsp;
Kaidou commented that Luffy is vulnerable to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:52.320
slicing attacks in Gear 5th. Obviously, Luffy has&nbsp;
survived plenty of cuts, but since this weakness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:58.960
is explicitly stated so many times, the fruit&nbsp;
was docked 3 points in the weakness category.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:07.520
**And that’s unfortunate for Luffy, because&nbsp;
coming in at #1 with 96 points - just two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.480
more than the Nika fruit…is the&nbsp;
Tori Tori no Mi: Model Phoenix!**

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.880
Marco’s fruit gained 22 points for strength and&nbsp;
24 points for durability. While not the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:28.480
physically powerful zoan, his regenerative&nbsp;
properties assisted a bit with his durability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:34.480
Given that he was just fine holding his own&nbsp;
against both King and Queen, two powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:40.480
ancient zoans with immense raw strength,&nbsp;
it made sense to rate these areas highly.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:48.000
His special abilities received a perfect score&nbsp;
of 25 as well. Not only does he have the enviable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:57.040
ability of flight, but he can use his flames to&nbsp;
heal others as well. This also gives him a perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:02.960
score in the everyday use category because being&nbsp;
able to heal others would be a wonderful trait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:08.720
to have in the real world. Any hospital would be&nbsp;
lucky to have Marco the Phoenix on their staff.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:14.160
If it turns out that like the mythical phoenix,&nbsp;
Marco is even able to revive from death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:19.280
this score may become even higher one day.&nbsp;
But until then, it’s just speculation. With no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:25.520
weaknesses or drawbacks to speak of, the Phoenix&nbsp;
is the greatest zoan devil fruit in One Piece.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:31.360
It just so happens that these five powerful&nbsp;
zoans are only exclusively of the mythivcal type,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:35.760
but just like Luffy’s real fruit&nbsp;
was only revealed late in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:40.400
that might be true for another character as&nbsp;
well, Blackbeard. If you want to find out why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:47.840
he might make it onto this list very very soon,&nbsp;
you should really not miss out on this video here.

